      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "so it's 2024, it's furality, instances can get up to 70 people, and even if I run with showing only thew nearest 6 avis (+ 3 friends) within 10 meters, I realiably crash after enough people came into and out of the radius. That is after VRChat took \"only\" 15-16 GB of VRAM (7 just to start mind you) and my RAM usage went up to about 24GB out of 32GB. I have a 7900 XTX, and VRChat isn't freeing up ANY VRAM after people left my radius. It is also dissapointing that VRChat isn't able to use more than those 16GB of VRAM mentioned. Same thing happens when trying to take 8K photos in worlds that don't have just me in it, since VRAM ballons to 16GB for a bit, and then crashes. This was working without issue before on the same GPU. I've also stress tested my VRAM, all 24GB of it are functional.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
